WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.474
Not every download has to start right now.

2
00:00:02.474 --> 00:00:07.952
Sometimes it's better to schedule it for the night, or when your data quota is more generous.

3
00:00:07.952 --> 00:00:12.429
In the New download window, fill in the Start at field with a date and time.

4
00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:16.375
You can pick a time a few minutes from now, or several hours ahead.

5
00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:21.618
Arus keeps the download in the queue and starts it automatically when the moment arrives.

6
00:00:21.618 --> 00:00:25.034
You can schedule several files with different start times.

7
00:00:25.034 --> 00:00:29.511
Downloads that aren't due yet wait in the queue without blocking the others.

8
00:00:29.511 --> 00:00:32.927
Open the Scheduled category to see every plan in one list.

9
00:00:32.927 --> 00:00:35.401
Each item shows its start time and status.

10
00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:38.582
It's great for large files you don't want to wait for.

11
00:00:38.582 --> 00:00:43.000
Your PC needs to stay on, and Arus needs to keep running in the background.

12
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.122
You don't have to reopen the app when the time comes.

13
00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:50.010
Arus does the work and sends a notification when the file is done.

14
00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:53.838
So a big download can run without getting in the way of your day.

